 the tunnel; after N successive failures (default 3) it fires a recovery callback wired to an
 Xray restart.
 
+### 5.9 AmneziaWG in-process backend
+
+AmneziaWG (obfuscated WireGuard) cannot be served by the stock Xray-core binary (plain
+`wireguard-go`, no obfuscation), so — like MTProto — it runs **outside** Xray. Unlike MTProto it
+needs **no sidecar binary**: `internal/awg/` embeds the `amnezia-vpn/amneziawg-go` library on a
+userspace gVisor netstack (the same technique as Xray's own WireGuard inbound), so it needs no root,
+no kernel module, and works in unprivileged Docker.
+
+- **`internal/awg/`**: `params.go` (obfuscation knobs Jc/Jmin/Jmax, S1–S4, H1–H4, I1–I5 + validation +
+  randomized defaults + UAPI/`.conf` rendering), `netstack.go` + `forwarder.go` (a forwarding gVisor
+  stack that carries decrypted client traffic to the host, fenced by `internal/util/netsafe`),
+  `device.go` (amneziawg-go device lifecycle + per-peer stats), `manager.go` (one device per inbound;
+  fingerprint decides restart vs. live peer update), `config.go` (`InstanceFromInbound`).
+- **Excluded from Xray config** in `service/xray.go` (a `continue` next to the MTProto skip).
+- **Dispatched** through `runtime/local.go` (AddInbound→Ensure, DelInbound→Remove); per-client changes
+  converge via the reconcile job.
+- **Reconcile + traffic**: `job/awg_job.go` (`@every 10s`), registered in `web.go` `startTask`;
+  `StopAll` on shutdown. Folds per-inbound and per-client traffic via `inboundService.AddTraffic`.
+- Reuses the **WireGuard client model** (no DB migration); classified UDP in `port_conflict.go`.
+
+See `docs/amneziawg.md` for the operator-facing guide and verification steps.
+
 ---
 
